{"name":"Bollywood","hex":"#debb32","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bollywood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Hindi-language film industry located in Mumbai.","The cinema of India in general, no matter the region."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bollywood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hindi cinema","blocks":[{"text":"Hindi cinema, popularly known as Bollywood, refers to India's Hindi-language film industry, based in Mumbai. The popular term Bollywood is a portmanteau of \"Bombay\" and \"Hollywood\". The industry, producing films in the Hindi language, is a part of the larger Indian cinema industry, which also includes South Indian cinema and other smaller film industries. The term 'Bollywood', often mistakenly used to refer to Indian cinema as a whole, only refers to Hindi-language films, with Indian cinema being an umbrella term that includes all the film industries in the country, each offering films in diverse languages and styles."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindi_cinema","wikidata":"Q93196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Phalke.jpg/500px-Phalke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Phalke.jpg/500px-Phalke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dadasaheb Phalke is considered the father of Indian cinema, including Hindi cinema.[20][21][22]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhalke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Hindi_movie_production_trend.pdf/page1-500px-Hindi_movie_production_trend.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Hindi_movie_production_trend.pdf/page1-1280px-Hindi_movie_production_trend.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p